#
# Five optimisation hypotheses, tested in order. Only the last one holds:
#   1. dQ fp32 atomicAdd contention .......... 0.1-8%   (NO_ATOMIC diagnostic build)
#   2. MAC rate: half2 on S/dP and dQ ........ +13%     AND fails regimes 2+4 badly
#   3. dV/dK shared fragment count (1cx16k -> 2cx8k) .. +0.2%
#   4. __half2float count (hoist out of the pairing loop) .. 0% (ptxas already CSE'd it)
#   5. global traffic: BC 32 -> 64, halving Q/dO re-reads .. +6.8%  <-- the real one
#
# So the backward is GLOBAL-MEMORY-TRAFFIC bound, not compute, not atomics.
# Recompute economics, closing the loop on the corrected break-even at the top
# of PLAN.md: threshold 16.0 TFLOPS at d=64, backward achieves 3.16, so
# recomputing S should cost ~5.1x what storing and reloading it would.
# Measured: recompute 34.4 GFLOP / 3.16 TF = 10.9 ms vs 1.07 GB / 499 GB/s =
# 2.15 ms to store+reload. Ratio 5.1x. The formula predicted it exactly.
#
