#
# --- Backward optimisation round 2, 2026-09-07: read the SASS instead of guessing ---
#
# Four hypotheses had already died (atomics, half2-in-outer-products, tile
# reshape, conversion hoisting). Rather than invent a fifth, counted the actual
# instruction mix with `cuobjdump -sass`:
#
#   6473 instructions in bwd_kernel<64,64,64,128>
#     FFMA   1856  28.7%   <- the actual math
#     HADD2   864  13.3%   <- __half2float. Pascal compiles it to
#                             HADD2.F32 Rd, Rs.H0_H0, -RZ.H0_H0
#     XMAD/MOV/IADD/LEA/SHR/ISETP  1772  27.4%  <- address arithmetic
#   math 49.9% | address 27.4%
#
# So it is ISSUE bound -- 3.5 instructions per useful FMA -- and the
# conversions are a seventh of the whole kernel. That also retires the
# "global-traffic bound" reading from the first round: BC 32->64 helped, but
# the instruction stream is the real ceiling.
#
# THE FIX. The earlier half2 experiment had applied __hfma2 to the OUTER
# products (S/dP and dQ) -- exactly where dS = P*(dP - D) cancellation lives --
# and got +13% with regimes 2/4 blown out to ~1e0. The dV/dK CONTRACTION is the
